-**Edge Cases and Pitfalls**
-*   **Perturbation Strength:** Using excessively strong worst-case perturbations (e.g., PGD-10) deteriorates training performance instead of improving it [S1].
-*   **Feature Injection Point:** Injecting perturbation into the middle layer of NeRF’s MLP contributes the most significantly to performance gains [S1].
-*   **Batch Size:** The algorithm description assumes a batch size of 1 for simplicity [S1].
-*   **Precision:** Perturbations must be clamped to ensure color and density values remain within valid ranges (e.g., $[0, 1]$) [S1].
 
